# UI primitives

Follow [.llm/ui-primitives.md](mdc:.llm/ui-primitives.md). Colors: [.llm/color-palette.md](mdc:.llm/color-palette.md) §0.

## Imports — concrete files only

```tsx
import { AppText } from '@/src/components/common/AppText';
import { AppTextV2 } from '@/src/components/common/AppTextV2';
import { AppButton } from '@/src/components/common/AppButton';
import { AppButtonV2 } from '@/src/components/common/AppButtonV2';
import { ScreenWrapper } from '@/src/components/common/ScreenWrapper';
```

Do **not** add `index.ts` barrels that re-export “latest” as the default `AppText` / `AppButton`.

## When to use

| Primitive | Use |
| :--- | :--- |
| `AppText` | Default product copy (`variant` + color via `className`) |
| `AppTextV2` | Semantic `colorScheme` (CVA); `secondary` = muted body, not white CTA |
| `AppButton` / `AppButtonV2` | CTAs; icons via `renderIcon={(c,s) => <Iconify icon="…" … />}` |
| `ScreenWrapper` | Full screens owning safe area + status bar |
| `AppInput` / `AppBottomSheet` / `AppImage(V2)` | Prefer over one-off RN primitives |

## ScreenWrapper

- **Do:** onboarding, dashboard shell, standalone routes.
- **Do not:** bottom sheets, modals, nested content already inside tab/stack chrome.
- `withPadding` default `true`; `false` for full-bleed.
- `backgroundColor` (camelCase) fills SafeAreaView **including the phone status-bar strip**. `className` does not.
- Defaults follow theme canvas; metallic slate heroes pass a dark slate stop + `statusBarStyle="light-content"` (not `COLORS.*.brand.primary` in dark — that is the light CTA fill).
- Never write `backgroundcolor` — prop is ignored → white notification row.

## Do

```tsx
<AppText variant="h3" className="text-text-primary">Title</AppText>
<AppText className="text-text-primary-lighter">Meta</AppText>

<AppTextV2 variant="body-small" colorScheme="secondary">Muted</AppTextV2>

<AppButton variant="primary" renderIcon={(c) => <Iconify icon="heroicons:plus-circle" size={18} color={c} />}>
  Create
</AppButton>

// Neutral screen
<ScreenWrapper
  backgroundColor={isDark ? COLORS.dark.bg.primary : COLORS.light.bg.primary}
  statusBarStyle={isDark ? 'light-content' : 'dark-content'}
>
  {children}
</ScreenWrapper>

// Metallic slate hero — status bar matches dark chrome
<ScreenWrapper
  backgroundColor={isDark ? '#0F172A' : '#1E293B'}
  statusBarStyle="light-content"
  withPadding={false}
>
  {children}
</ScreenWrapper>
```

## Do not

```tsx
// Version-picking barrel
import { AppText } from '@/src/components/common/features/AppText';

// Raw Text for product UI (prefer AppText / AppTextV2)
<Text className="text-lg">Title</Text>

// White CTA token as muted body
<AppText className="text-text-secondary">Loading more...</AppText>

// Wrong prop case → white status bar strip
<ScreenWrapper backgroundcolor={COLORS.light.brand.primary} />

// className alone does not paint the notification row
<ScreenWrapper className="bg-bg-secondary" />

// ScreenWrapper around sheet / modal body
<AppBottomSheet><ScreenWrapper>{…}</ScreenWrapper></AppBottomSheet>
```

## Also

- Iconify `icon` = string literal (see iconify-string-literals rule).
- Sheet portal pitfalls: [.llm/exceptions.md](mdc:.llm/exceptions.md).
- Private UI stays under `src/screens/…`; promote to `src/components/` only on a second consumer.
